    there's certainly no copyright infringement using the basic
    ideas (i.e. gremlins multipying in water), regardless of
    where they come from.

 -- Just a word isn't copyrightable, so things like "mithril"
    and "mumak" shouldn't pose problems.  (A complete
    "character" is copyrightable, of course.  But I don't think
    that mumakil are characterized enough in Tolkien to
    qualify.)

Of course, if a copyright holder has good enough lawyers, and
wants to bother, you can probably be taken to court for just
about anything, at least in the U.S.

